<title>USA: Clinton would sunset tax cuts to balance budget.</title>
<headline>Clinton would sunset tax cuts to balance budget.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton's budget called for most of his proposed $98 billion in tax cuts to be repealed if necessary to bring the budget into balance by 2002.</p>
<p>In addition, if the White House economic forecasts prove overly optimistic and the deficit were to increase, his plan would levy across the board spending cuts on both entitlements and annual discretionary spending to balance the budget.</p>
</text>
